course: dictionary
lesson: 2127
title: Convincing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Convincing» has a few meanings, and the words around it tell you which one. In «a convincing argument», it means something that makes you believe it is true or right. Good reasons and evidence make an argument convincing.
explain: In «a convincing win», it means clear and complete, so nobody doubts who won. Ask yourself what the rest of the sentence is about: a reason someone should believe something, or a result that is big and clear?
explain: Convincing can also be a verb form of «convince», which means persuading someone. «She is convincing her mum to get a dog» means she is trying to make her mum agree. Try swapping in "persuading" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Be careful with things that look convincing but are not true. In one story, a plan is called «not very convincing artifice», where artifice means a trick that did not fool anyone. Scam messages can look convincing too, so check with an adult before you click.
fact: Convincing means making you believe something is true or right.
fact: «A convincing argument» uses good reasons and evidence.
fact: «A convincing win» is a big, clear win with no doubt about the result.
fact: «Not very convincing» means a trick or story did not fool anyone well.
fact: Scam messages can look convincing, so check with an adult before you click.
exercise: «Her argument used three clear reasons and real evidence.» What kind of argument is it? | A glum argument | An ancient argument | *A convincing argument | A barely argument
exercise: «The team won by ten goals to none.» What does convincing mean in «a convincing win»? | Short and rude | Only just | *Clear and complete | Very old
exercise: «She is convincing her mum to get a dog.» What is convincing doing here? | Cleaning up | Falling asleep | Making a loud noise | *Persuading someone
test: «The scam message looked so convincing that Dad nearly clicked the link.» What does convincing mean here? | Very funny | *Looking real enough to be believed | Short and rude | Only just
test: Which word means persuading someone to believe something? | *convince | curt | ancient | famished
exam: Which is the best explanation of the difference between «a convincing argument» and «a convincing win»? | *An argument makes you believe something is true; a win is big and clear | Both mean exactly the same thing | An argument is a fight and a win is a prize | Convincing means very old
